# Nicanzil, Current Conductor {G}{U}: "Whenever a creature you control explores a land card, you may put a land card from your hand onto the battlefield tapped"
# (CR 701.44a, 603.2, 614.1c). Bot1's Cenote Scout explores an Island, which goes to the hand, and the trigger resolves after: the hand holds a Plains, a Lightning Bolt and
# that Island. The Bolt is refused (not a land card), and the Island itself is chosen: it enters tapped, the Plains stays, and putting it is not playing it, so
# Bot1's land play (the Forest) is the only one used. Bot2's hand of Islands is not a choice and stays put.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Nicanzil, Current Conductor
Cenote Scout
Forest
Plains
Lightning Bolt
Island
Mountain
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Nicanzil, Current Conductor.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Cenote Scout.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
Bot1.Choose(Island)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Tapped = true
? Bot1.LandsPlayed = 1

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Cenote Scout; Forest; Island; Mox Emerald; Mox Sapphire; Nicanzil, Current Conductor
Bot1.Hand = Lightning Bolt; Plains
Bot1.Battlefield.Nicanzil, Current Conductor.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
Bot2.Hand.Count = 7
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
